# Deploy to Vercel after updates

When you finish a user-requested change that should go live (UI, copy, pages, content, styles), deploy it to Vercel production before you stop. Do not wait for the user to ask again.

## How

This repo is linked to Vercel project `usegrokbot` (team `aipost`) via `.vercel/project.json`. There is no git remote. Use the CLI, not git push:

```bash
vercel deploy --prod -y --no-wait --scope aipost
vercel inspect <deployment-url>
```

Then give the user the production URL (`https://usegrokbot.com` and the deployment URL).

## Do not

- Deploy unrelated local experiments or half-finished work
- Change Vercel env vars, domains, or project settings as part of a normal deploy
- Skip deploy because the change looks small. If it is on the live site, ship it.
